  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Narges Mohammadi (Persian: نرگس محمدی; born 21 April 1972) is an Iranian human rights activist and Nobel Peace Prize laureate. Between 1998 and October 2023, Mohammadi was arrested 13 times and sentenced to 31 years in prison and 154 lashes. She has been the recipient of many human rights awards. In October 2023, while in prison, she was awarded the 2023 Nobel Peace Prize \"for her fight against the oppression of women in Iran and her fight to promote human rights and freedom for all\".",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
